-- Ascension's Worldforged find locations.
--
-- The table is created by worldforged.sql, which the DB updater applies first
-- because it sorts module SQL by filename and '.' sorts before '_'.
--
-- GENERATED by tools/worldforged/build_ascension_spawns.py - re-run the tool
-- rather than editing this file.
--
-- Decoded from the LootCollector addon's community starter database in the
-- Ascension client and converted from zone percentages to world coordinates the
-- same way the core's Zone2MapCoordinates() does. Verified against this world
-- database: the median point lands 16 yards from the nearest creature spawn.
--
-- Several players finding the same chest each produced their own recording,
-- so entries of the same item within a few yards are merged into one -
-- otherwise the world gets three chests side by side where Ascension has one.
--
-- `item` is the Worldforged item Ascension players actually found at that spot.
-- There is no Z: ground height needs the server's map data and is resolved with
-- Map::GetHeight() when the cache is streamed in.
--
-- 1633 locations. 351 finds were dropped: they sit in caves,
-- mines and starting sub-zones, whose percentages are relative to a sub-map with
-- no WorldMapArea row and so cannot be converted.

DELETE FROM `mod_madosa_worldforged_ascension_spawns`;
